Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:36:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] r4-prep 3/3: first lakeside entry - the board reuses the
 journey copy's merged geometry instead of rebuilding it in the entry frame

Code-path analysis of the first-entry worst frame (Mac 133 ms day / 115 night; no device here): the board load runs synchronously in one
tick after the cached bundle: 431-instance instantiate, instancing copies, water material copy and the static merge (~58k vertices:
decode + world-space append + utils.createMesh + upload). A node bench of the JS part alone is ~30-45 ms on desktop; with readAttribute
copies and createMesh it is the largest single CPU block. Since b449fc1 the journey copy merges the SAME scene during the loading bar,
baked relative to the scenery root, so the geometry is identical: mergeLakesideStatic now publishes its meshes with a signature (per
chunk: instance name, source mesh, primitive, vertex count, local placement) and a later identical merge reuses them (refcounted handle
per merge; last holder destroys; mismatch -> fresh merge; failed merge never touches shared meshes). Board entry skips the rebuild and
the second ~1.6 MB copy. Same draws, same materials, ?lakemerge=off unchanged. Test lakeside-merge-share.
